BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mazon Creek: Illinois' Tropical History
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260717T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260717T130000
DTSTAMP:20260714T095932Z
UID:10038d1f8a4e9edcba580a98c7047f16@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nThe Mazon Creek region is a f
 ossil rich area approximately 60 miles away from Chicago.  Fossil hunters
  have traveled there for decades to search for evidence of what life looke
 d like long ago. The fossil evidence paints a picture of a 300 million yea
 r old tropical forest adjacent to a shallow marine environment. Join membe
 rs of ESCONI\, the Earth Science Club of Northern Illinois  including Jer
 emy Zimmerman (Field Trip Coordinator)\, Rich Holm (Historian/Web Administ
 rator)\, and Jack Wittry (Field Museum Collections Associate) as they reco
 unt some of their own discoveries in Mazon\, and showcase the plants and a
 nimals of ancient Illinois.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/ou
 r-events/meet-a-scientist/mazon-creek-illinois-tropical-history
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/mazon-creek-il
 linois-tropical-history
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Mazon Creek: Illinois' Tropical History
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Mazon Creek: Illinois' Tropical History
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
